000000009001000000000440001254696d6573204e657720526f6d616e0000000000000000000000000000000000040000002d01000004000000020101000500
00000902000000020d000000320a5a00ffff01000400ffff0000670e0d0020f32d00030000001e0008000000fa0200000600000000000000040000002d010100
07000000fc020100000000000000040000002d0102000800000025030200040003005f0e030008000000fa0200000000000000000000040000002d0103000700
0000fc020000ffffff000000040000002d01040004000000f0010100040000002701ffff1c000000fb021000070000000000bc02000000000102022253797374656d000000000000fd99807c58bd1e0010f9230070bb1e005ae78339040000002d010100030000000000}}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f1\insrsid8014045  World Bank suggests some structural reform policies for the poor countries to grow. Discuss those policies briefly.
\par Ans:
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\insrsid8014045 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\cf1\insrsid8014045 World Bank has suggested following policies for the poor countries to grow,
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid8014045 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\ul\cf1\insrsid8014045 Governance and administrative reforms:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid8014045  
\par To reduce over employment in public sector, reduce wastes and to improve the quality and reliability of public services. To strengthen the administration of taxes, to eliminate the corruption. To decent
ralize the control of fiscal policy making. To enrich the legal and regulator framework.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\ul\cf1\insrsid8014045 Privatization of state-owned enterprises:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid8014045  Abbreviated as SOEs. These are influenced by political interference and it is one of the reasons SOEs are considered ineffic
ient. SOEs are also suffering form lack of competition, cost awareness and fear of bankruptcy.
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\ul\cf1\insrsid8014045 Financial liberalization:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid8014045   It involves ending of financial repression policies including artificially low interest rates, credit rationing, restrictions on banking competition and government involvement in investment allocation

\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\ul\cf1\insrsid8014045 Deregulation involving dismantling of licensing systems and red-tape}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid8014045 
\par  }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\ul\cf1\insrsid8014045 Trade liberalization:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid8014045  
\par including tariffication of non-tariff-barriers, harmonization of tariffs and an eventual reduction thereof
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\ul\cf1\insrsid8014045 FDI liberalization:  
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid8014045 To create a transparent, predictable environment for foreign investors to operate in. 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\ul\cf1\insrsid8014045 apital account liberalization:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid8014045  
\par  To remove controls on capital flows
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\tx1320\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\cf1\insrsid8014045 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \cf1\insrsid8014045 (These policies are suggested by world bank and the successful implementation of these policies depend on the political and economic system of poor countries. In general these policies a
re expected to provide the poor nation with better understanding and help them to raise their growth.)}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\cf1\insrsid8014045 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid8014045     }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid8014045 
\par Question No: 50    ( Marks: 3 ) 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid14549560 {\pict{\*\picprop\shplid1035{\sp{\sn shapeType}{\sv 75}}{\sp{\sn fFlipH}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fFlipV}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLine}{\sv 0}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}{\sp{\sn fLayoutInCell}{\sv 1}}}
