\b\f1\insrsid8014045  Explain the difference between endogenous growth model and exogenous growth model.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid8014045 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid8014045     }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid8014045 
\par Question No: 52    ( Marks: 5 ) 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\ul\insrsid8014045 EXOGENOUS GROWTH THEORY}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\insrsid8014045 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 The Exogenous growth model, also known as the Neo-classical growth model or Solow growth model is
\par a term used to sum up the contributions of various authors to a model of long-run economic growth
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 within the framework of neoclassical economics}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 
\ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid8014045  
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\ul\insrsid8014045 ENDOGENOUS GROWTH THEORY}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f41\fs22\insrsid8014045 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 In economics, }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\insrsid8014045 endogenous growth theory }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 or }{\rtlch\fcs1 
\ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\insrsid8014045 new growth theory }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 was developed in the 1980s as a
\par response to criticism of the neo-classical growth model.
\par In neoclassical growth models, the long-run rate of growth is exogenously determined by assuming a
\par savings rate (the Solow model) or a rate of technical progress. This does not explain the origin of
\par growth, which makes the neo-classical model appear very unrealistic. Endogenous growth theorists see
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 this as an over-simplification}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 
\b\f1\insrsid8014045 
\par 
\par Following table shows different stages of production of cloth. Calculate the value added at each stage of production. What is GDP by this approach?
\par \ltrrow}\trowd \irow0\irowband0\ltrrow\ts11\trgaph108\trleft-108\trftsWidth1\trpaddl108\trpaddr108\trpaddfl3\trpaddfr3\tblind0\tblindtype3 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrl\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrb\brdrs\brdrw15 \clbrdrr\brdrs\brdrw15 
