\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\insrsid8014045 
\par     }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\ul\cf5\insrsid8014045 REFERENCE
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\insrsid8014045 METHODS OF MEASURING GDP
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 There are three equivalent ways of measuring GDP:
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\insrsid8014045 i. The product or value added method }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 which sums the value added by all the productive
\par entities in the economy;
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\insrsid8014045 ii. The expenditure method }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 which sums up the value of all the \'93final goods\'94 transactions
\par taking place in the economy;
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs22\insrsid8014045 iii. The factor income method }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 which sums up all the incomes earned by all the factors of
\par production in the economy (rent for land, wages for labour, interest for capital, and equity
\par returns for entrepreneurship).
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af41\afs28 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f41\fs28\insrsid8014045 Value added }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af39\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \f39\fs22\insrsid8014045 is the difference between the value of goods produced and the cost of materials and
\par supplies used in producing them. Value added consists of the wages, interest and profit components
\par added to the output by a firm. Value added is the difference between inputs and outputs e-g if a firm
\par spends Rs.500 making a good (inputs) and sells its product (output) for Rs.750, then value added is
\par Rs.250.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid8014045 
\par 
\par Question No: 53    ( Marks: 5 ) 
\par }\pard \ltrpar\qj \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs20\insrsid14549560 
