\b\f1\insrsid8014045  Why countries have comparative advantage according to Ricardo?}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af1\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \f1\fs32\cf1\insrsid8014045 
\par        
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs32\cf1\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid8014045 ANSWER:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs32 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs32\ul\cf1\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid8014045 
\par 
\par Comparative advantage according to Ricardo:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\ul\cf2\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid8014045 
\par 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid8014045 The law of }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid8014045 comparative advantage}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid8014045 
 refers to the ability of a party (an individual, a firm, or a country) to produce a particular good or service at a lower }{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid8014045 opportunity cost t}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid8014045 han another party.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid8014045  There is a  source of comparative advantage can be productivity differentials.}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 
\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid8014045 Ricardo argued that there is mutual benefit from trade (or exchange) even if one party }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid8014045 
(e.g. resource rich country, highly-skilled artisan}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \lang9\langfe1033\langnp9\insrsid8014045 ) is more productive in every possible 
area than its trading counterpart (e.g. resource-poor country, unskilled laborer), as long as each concentrates on the activities where it has a relative productivity advantage}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \insrsid8014045 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\insrsid8014045 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af1 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\f1\insrsid8014045 Question No: 51    ( Marks: 5 ) 
