\b\f1\insrsid8014045  "Slope of the consumption function is less than 1".What is meant by this statement?  
\par }\pard \ltrpar\ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault{\*\pn \pnlvlcont\ilvl0\ls0\pnrnot0\pndec }\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\insrsid8014045 
\par }{\rtlch\fcs1 \ab\af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \b\fs22\cf1\insrsid8014045 ANSWER:}{\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs22 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs22\cf1\insrsid8014045 
\par When we drawn in expenditure income space, the consumption function plots as a straight line with positive intercept, and a positive but less than 1 slope. The slope is less than 1 because not all the income is consumed some part of the income is saved.}{
\rtlch\fcs1 \af0\afs20 \ltrch\fcs0 \fs20\cf1\insrsid8014045 
